#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:112
msgid "Memory Management"
msgstr "Gestione della Memoria"

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:113
msgid ""
"**🚨 CRITICAL: Always use proper RAII patterns - smart pointers, moveable "
"objects, or wrapper classes instead of raw pointers for resource "
"management.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:115
msgid "**Resource Management Options:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:116
msgid ""
"✅ **PREFERRED**: `fl::shared_ptr<T>` for shared ownership (multiple "
"references to same object)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:117
msgid ""
"✅ **PREFERRED**: `fl::unique_ptr<T>` for exclusive ownership (single "
"owner, automatic cleanup)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:118
msgid ""
"✅ **PREFERRED**: Moveable wrapper objects (like `fl::promise<T>`) for "
"safe copying and transferring of unique resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:119
msgid ""
"✅ **ACCEPTABLE**: `fl::vector<T>` storing objects by value when objects "
"support move/copy semantics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:120
msgid ""
"❌ **AVOID**: `fl::vector<T*>` storing raw pointers - use "
"`fl::vector<fl::shared_ptr<T>>` or `fl::vector<fl::unique_ptr<T>>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/AGENTS.md:121
msgid ""
"❌ **AVOID**: Manual `new`/`delete` - use `fl::make_shared<T>()` or "
"`fl::make_unique<T>()`"
msgstr ""

