#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:169
msgid ""
"Subsequent agents can give a brief summary of the WLED-MM-P4 Parallel IO "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:171
msgid "Comments on Parlios 20us random delay glitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:173
msgid ""
"Byte boundaries are super important! If we split on say the nibble, then "
"this can trigger a corruption on any order bit. If we split on the byte "
"boundary, the worst that can happen is that the low order byte is "
"possibly corrupted. What does the data manual say about this? It should "
"be investigated by one of the agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:176
msgid "Someone said..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:178
msgid ""
"This is a demo of the WLED-MM-P4 Parallel IO driver in action with 16x512"
" pixels driven:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:180
msgid "https://www.reddit.com/r/WLED/s/q1pZg1mnwZ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:182
msgid ""
"Which looking at the FastLED Parallel IO code should be essentially the "
"same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:184
msgid ""
"@zackees the benefit I found to supporting 1/2/4/8/16-bit depths is the "
"idle period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:186
msgid ""
"For example - if you have 2 pins it's better to use 2-bit widths because "
"it's ~5460 RGB LEDs per transmit no matter what your bit width is - so at"
" 1/2/4-bit widths you're almost guaranteed to never have a glitch because"
" of a DMA delay between transmits (assuming like 1024 LEDs max per pin). "
"Transmits are also faster if you match bit-width to pin counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:188
msgid ""
"My demo has 512x16 so it's 2 buffers being sent and there's a small gap "
"visible on my logic analyzer. As long as that's below about 20us (even "
"tho the spec sheets say 50us) it doesn't glitch - but above that I've had"
" to work hard to keep things from making the pause longer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../FastLED_Sphinx/source/examples/Validation/ai_prompt.md:190
msgid ""
"I also break my buffers so it's after the LSB of the triplet (or quad). "
"In case that pause is misnterpreted as a 1 vs 0, it's not going to cause "
"a visual disruption. At worst 0,0,0 becomes 0,0,1."
msgstr ""

